WEBVTT

NOTE whisper small.en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.770
Hi, welcome to this course on how to structure your machine learning project, that is, on

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.690
machine learning strategy.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.090
I hope that through this course, you learn how to much more quickly and efficiently get

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.570
your machine learning systems working.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.130
So what is machine learning strategy?

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.890
Let's start with a motivating example.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:26.410
Let's say you are working on your CAD classifier, and after working for some time, you've gotten

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:32.170
your system to have 90% accuracy, but this isn't good enough for your application.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.070
You might then have a lot of ideas for how to improve your system.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.450
For example, you might think, well, let's collect more data, more training data.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:43.250
Or you might say, maybe your training set isn't diverse enough yet, you should collect

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:49.570
images of cats in more diverse poses, or maybe a more diverse set of negative examples.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.250
Or maybe you want to train the algorithm longer with gradient descends, or maybe you want

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.690
to try a different optimization algorithm, like the Adam optimization algorithm.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.730
Or maybe try a bigger network, or a smaller network.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:05.490
Or maybe you want to try Dropout, or maybe L2 regularization.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:09.890
Or maybe you want to change the network architecture, such as trying the activation functions,

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.930
change the number of fitting units, and so on and so on.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:17.450
When trying to improve a deep learning system, you often have a lot of ideas for things

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.330
you could try.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.850
And the problem is that if you choose poorly, it's entirely possible that you end up spending

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.650
six months charging in some direction, only to realize after six months that that didn't

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.890
do any good.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:35.170
For example, I've seen some teams spend literally six months collecting more data,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:40.410
only to realize after six months that it barely improved the performance of their system.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.970
So assuming you don't have six months to waste on your problem, wouldn't it be nice

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.810
if you had quick and effective ways to figure out which of all of these ideas, and maybe

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:54.730
even other ideas, are worth pursuing, and which ones you can safely discard.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.730
So what I hope to do in this course is teach you a number of strategies, that is ways of

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:04.690
analyzing machine learning problem, that will point you in the direction of the most promising

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.690
things to try.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.610
What I'll do in this course is also share with you a number of lessons I've learned

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:14.010
through building and shipping, you know, large number of deep learning products.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.730
And I think these materials are actually quite unique to this course.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:22.450
I don't see a lot of these ideas being taught in universities deep learning courses, for

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.010
example.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:29.050
It turns out also that machine learning strategy is changing in the era of deep learning because

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:33.690
the things you could do are now different with deep learning algorithms than with previous

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.930
generation of machine learning algorithms.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.770
But I hope that these ideas will help you become much more effective at getting your

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.330
deep learning systems to work.
